        "original_id": "eba65d8e-25f5-5cbc-82a3-183907877d00",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Queens, Queens County, Staten Island, Flushing Meadows–Corona Park, Flushing Bay, LaGuardia Airport\n- Systems: I-678 (Van Wyck Expressway), Grand Central Parkway\n- Topics: population, area, foreign-born residents\n\nFacts:\n- Since 1899, the borough of Queens has been coterminous with Queens County.\n- In 2016, Queens had a census-estimated population of 2,333,054, making it the second-largest New York City borough by population after Brooklyn.\n- In 2016, approximately 48% of Queens residents were foreign-born.\n- In 2016, Staten Island had a census-estimated population of 476,015, making it the least populated New York City borough.\n- Staten Island is the third-largest New York City borough by area at 58 square miles.\n- Flushing Meadows–Corona Park is located in Queens between I-678 (Van Wyck Expressway) and the Grand Central Parkway.\n- Flushing Meadows–Corona Park stretches from Flushing Bay at the southern edge of LaGuardia Airport to Union Turnpike.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
